{"title":"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df7a2b3bc10bb227095c5b95a525c534228c1d34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{13} = w,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f260cf0a28edf333ebb5fb573777e46dd1b4da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^{11} = z,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> and the imaginary part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a6111b79145a12c0134dc04557ec3770de4ca9bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\frac{m\\pi}{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"34\" />, for relatively prime positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fdf225f571367cfdd6340aa01061d0e173ce75a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&lt;n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"10\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Substituting the first equation into the second, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/499bbec55fa5a706ff50e13f6b38a5aa5602927c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z^{13})^{11} = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/85290c5a13e592e0802ece6c36e7d3819e527902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{143} = z.$\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" /> We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6d73454d2953bc17507cbd59f4ece4b3b41796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\neq 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> since we are given the imaginary part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so we can divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc9d80e9e07cb4acc9f52ab648b2540e5376ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{142} = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8614c1b3993e78519131182767d0a43ea0714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />nd root of unity, and thus, by De Moivre's theorem, the imaginary part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> will be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f462b28641f6a1cd14ffeccfaf51a440c61a2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\frac{2k\\pi}{142}} = \\sin{\\frac{k\\pi}{71}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9bf08266e12b28d68e12ca062da27979ced7cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 70\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c4bc29a5a0d6756b52b0277d9cd07e756225c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcbc86905142d54cac7dd8ecf08921c70a3524.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;71$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> by the conditions of the problem, so the denominator in the argument of this value will always be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/118ca81f7695108cef1f2e48007084513dc1d20b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$71.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a363ad380cb1079988714246a387812d24ab6898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{071}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"81\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is similar to solution 1.\n</p><p>As before, determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e7d1aa7c55bc53487ec9d9c457703d9a458cca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{143} = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111369f8f4f058743130a02db1a744c75cbdbd2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{142} = 1 \\implies \\Im(z^{142}) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e04e54a3d8678f47b0d929097ac8bd1f231eb8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(142\\theta) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, which can only happen if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/a/15a309a5abe870cc90ebd20d4210a382174c265e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142\\theta = 2k\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916be879f6f793b63fae2bf2dd501afeeb0b3bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\frac{k\\pi}{71}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"39\" />. 71 is prime, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is relatively prime to all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c37b01d81e64c6030a2e9ef3cc97e15aa3521639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; 71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> through Euler Totient. Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/4742a0730b4183d73aa8322f4c81954ec8d0b5a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Im(z) = \\sin(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, so the requested imaginary part is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8c85474b8f44949226eac7b22e093fdaa32ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\frac{k\\pi}{71})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1376115e33ddd56cba2337a57e3013002ed284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{71}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Giving the same exponent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926677a61791c031462aace4dec86e0ce9b2cd94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{143}=w^{11}=z \\Longrightarrow z^{143}=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"220\" height=\"17\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aeaf56fb49067de712a3ad4f0f1d9dc86e162ec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> from the imaginary part. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/9282fc59d3bd59e2b2f5d0a6fbcdee4cbb822ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{142}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee1a2e68ab74f2bdb5aba0f51bf225ad1ce73e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142\\text{nd}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> root of unity. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a6ec87b81fcbbcb5c84d8666ee95f7e9c09643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=e^{\\frac{2\\pi i k}{142}}=e^{\\frac{\\pi i k}{71}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> Thus, comparing imaginary parts, we get,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5f3595ff495963b6e358acd3bfb4495f04978c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{\\dfrac{k\\pi}{71}}=\\sin{\\dfrac{m\\pi}{n}} \\Longrightarrow \\dfrac{k}{71}=\\dfrac{m}{n} \\Longrightarrow n=\\boxed{071}.\\]\" width=\"353\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cQmmkfZvPgU&amp;t=30s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cQmmkfZvPgU&amp;t=30s</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DMka35X-3WI&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvIo_foUDwmXnQClMHngjGto&amp;index=6\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DMka35X-3WI&amp;list=PLyhPcpM8aMvIo_foUDwmXnQClMHngjGto&amp;index=6</a> (Solution by Richard Rusczyk) - AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I\" title=\"2012 AIME I\">2012 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017225516\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 304/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8072/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.311      1 -total\n 58.05%    8.307      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.87%    5.706      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10859:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017225516 and revision id 286718. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}